ghOSt — third-party notices
===========================

ghOSt is an independent project, not a fork of any project listed here. A few of
its files adapt code or techniques from them — handtop in particular is a separate,
working build for the same hardware, used as a reference — and those notices are kept
here and in LICENSES/ so every copy of this source tree carries them.

1. handtop — https://github.com/junsulee119/handtop
   Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Handtop contributors
   Full text: LICENSES/MIT-handtop.txt
   Used for:
     - image/pack-image-rocknix.sh — the loop-free image assembly approach
       (build/10-image.sh): FAT boot partition as a file via mkfs.vfat + mtools,
       ext4 built with `mkfs.ext4 -d`, partitions dd'ed into an MBR image.
     - overlay/usr/local/sbin/ghost-panel — port of rg35xxh-panel (screen panel
       detection on board pin PE6).
     - overlay/usr/local/sbin/ghost-wifi-import — port of rg35xxh-wifi-import
       (Wi-Fi credentials from the boot partition).
     - image/bootfiles/{wifi.txt,panel.txt,README.txt} — the idea of editable
       provisioning files on the FAT partition.
   ghOSt changes are listed in each file's header: PARTUUID boot script rebuild,
   dual-panel DTB staging, host-identity stripping, ghOSt paths and systemd units.

